\par\b\fs28 \u167?7 Podcast rendering\b0\fs24\par


\par The image of the top shelf and the kitchen counter belongs to Nitzavim; here the image is different. Think of a sound that wakes you at night before you understand it: a child does not first sit up thinking, but at the calling of its name. The trumpet calls first; the understanding comes after. One physical image carries the landing: the clenched fist that becomes an open hand.\par



